  "description": "Encode DNA as phasor holograms whose geometry comes from measured DNA physics. Each base is a Phasor symbol face carried on a helical phase that advances by published, sequence-dependent dinucleotide twist (Olson et al. 1998, built in), optionally with a local DNA-shape layer (minor groove width, propeller twist, roll, helix twist) read from a pentamer table you supply. Windows of sequence become fixed-width vectors you can store in HoloDb, compare, or feed to any regression. Also grades sequences against your own measurements, with no files or console so it runs in a browser: a zero-parameter helical score, a cross-validated ridge readout on the holograms, and a fitted phasor model that reports the helical period (bases per turn), each with a correlation and a block-resampled 95% interval. Research and education only: it makes no health, disease-risk or drug-response claims. Experimental (0.x).",
